{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nGerrit 1876 patch set 2, GitHub Actions run 32193981982, Ubuntu Python 3.11 job 95894688032 failed after 13,892 tests passed. The session teardown fixture `tests/conftest.py::_remove_readonly_run_snapshots` evaluated `tuple(tmp_path.rglob(\".rebar/run_snapshots\"))`; traversal entered `repo/.tickets-tracker/.ticket-write.lock.d`, which disappeared during recursion, and `pathlib` raised `FileNotFoundError`. The failing node was `tests/interfaces/store/test_workflow_entrypoints.py::test_mcp_run_workflow_is_async_and_pollable`.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce the traversal failure with a deterministic barrier while separating three rivals: Python/pathlib version semantics, concurrent mkdir-lock churn, and fixture scope over the whole pytest temp tree.\n- Establish defect legitimacy and caller impact from the teardown contract and prior read-only snapshot cleanup bug.\n- Design a held-out race oracle at the smallest tier that executes the production teardown helper with real concurrent filesystem mutation; prove final-form RED.\n- Repair only the confirmed mechanism, then prove held-out GREEN, exact-defect mutation RED, and original-scenario replication.\n- Sweep all live recursive teardown scans for the same disappearing-entry hazard and disposition any siblings.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A runtime experiment deterministically proves the root cause and rejects pathlib-version-only and unrelated-fixture explanations.\n- [x] A gating regression test uses a deterministic synchronization barrier, reaches the disappearing-directory state, and asserts cleanup completes without masking unrelated filesystem errors.\n- [x] The final-form oracle is observed RED before repair, GREEN after a held-out repair, and RED again under an exact-defect mutation.\n- [x] Focused fixture/workflow tests, the broad relevant test gate, lint, and typecheck pass.\n- [x] All live recursive teardown scans are audited and every confirmed sibling is fixed or ticketed.\n- [x] The CI scenario no longer reproduces under repeated synchronized churn."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787101191635356001,"uuid":"a18ea26f-04de-482e-857b-3e70d4e58b2b"}